/// The props-type evidence of every member a lane's answer reaches: each prop it lists (`rows`, with its
/// `notableInherited` ones) in order, then each member of its collapsed `layers` it does not list. A member is ambient
/// when every declaration of it is: React's own, or one of the `private` sources its library marks private (ADR 0028:
/// by provenance, never by name); a member with no declaration is not.
/// `large` says whether the member is one of a generated set: a member of a layer (a source the resolver collapsed past
/// its thresholds), a member a mapped type copies from a large interface's keys
/// ([`ParsedProp::copied_from_large_keys`]), or a member of a source (its `parent`) that has a layer or reaches with
/// more than [`LARGE_API_SOURCE`] listed props. A listed prop with no `parent` has no known source and is large only when copied.
///
/// A member is own when the props type writes it, and overrides when, besides, a base declares it: its `parent` or a
/// declaration is not the props type, or a collapsed layer holds it.
#[cfg(test)]
pub(crate) fn members<'a>(
    props_type: &PropsType,
    rows: impl IntoIterator<Item = &'a ParsedProp>,
    layers: &[InheritedLayer],
    private: &BTreeMap<String, BTreeSet<String>>,
) -> Vec<Member> {
    members_but_quiet(props_type, rows, layers, private, |_| false).0
}

/// [`members`], except for the rows `quiet_candidate` takes that are quiet: a row whose own member, as its
/// declaration and the props type give it without any use, [`decide`](super::decide) leaves out
/// ([`super::listed_by_declaration`]). Each quiet row is returned apart, by name and whether it is ambient, and is no
/// [`Member`]: the caller has checked that no evidence of use names it, so it is left out as its member would be. It
/// still counts toward its source's reach and holds its name against a layer's member of the same name.
